{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1706","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Another String Minimization Problem"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You have a sequence $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$$$ of length $$$n$$$, consisting of integers between $$$1$$$ and $$$m$$$. You also have a string $$$s$$$, consisting of $$$m$$$ characters "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are going to perform the following $$$n$$$ operations. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" At the $$$i$$$-th ($$$1 \\le i \\le n$$$) operation, you replace either the $$$a_i$$$-th "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"or"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" the $$$(m + 1 - a_i)$$$-th character of $$$s$$$ with "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". You can replace the character at any position multiple times through the operations. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Find the lexicographically smallest string you can get after these operations."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A string $$$x$$$ is lexicographically smaller than a string $$$y$$$ of the same length if and only if in the first position where $$$x$$$ and $$$y$$$ differ, the string $$$x$$$ has a letter that appears earlier in the alphabet than the corresponding letter in $$$y$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains the number of test cases $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 2000$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$m$$$ ($$$1 \\le n, m \\le 50$$$) — the length of the sequence $$$a$$$ and the length of the string $$$s$$$ respectively."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$$$ ($$$1 \\le a_i \\le m$$$) — the sequence $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, print a string of length $$$m$$$ — the lexicographically smallest string you can get. Each character of the string should be either capital English letter "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" or capital English letter "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n6\n4 5\n1 1 3 1\n1 5\n2\n4 1\n1 1 1 1\n2 4\n1 3\n2 7\n7 5\n4 5\n5 5 3 5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nABABA\nBABBB\nA\nAABB\nABABBBB\nABABA\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, the sequence $$$a = [1, 1, 3, 1]$$$. One of the possible solutions is the following. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" At the $$$1$$$-st operation, you can replace the $$$1$$$-st character of $$$s$$$ with "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". After it, $$$s$$$ becomes "},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"BBBB"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" At the $$$2$$$-nd operation, you can replace the $$$5$$$-th character of $$$s$$$ with "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" (since $$$m+1-a_2=5$$$). After it, $$$s$$$ becomes "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ABBB"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" At the $$$3$$$-rd operation, you can replace the $$$3$$$-rd character of $$$s$$$ with "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". After it, $$$s$$$ becomes "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"AB"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"BA"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" At the $$$4$$$-th operation, you can replace the $$$1$$$-st character of $$$s$$$ with "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". After it, $$$s$$$ remains equal to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ABABA"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"kind":"text","text":" The resulting string is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ABABA"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". It is impossible to produce a lexicographically smaller string."},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, you are going to perform only one operation. You can replace either the $$$2$$$-nd character or $$$4$$$-th character of $$$s$$$ with "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". You can get strings "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"BABBB"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"BBBAB"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" after the operation. The string "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"BABBB"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the lexicographically smallest among these strings."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third test case, the only string you can get is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the fourth test case, you can replace the $$$1$$$-st and $$$2$$$-nd characters of $$$s$$$ with "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" to get "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"AABB"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the fifth test case, you can replace the $$$1$$$-st and $$$3$$$-rd characters of $$$s$$$ with "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" to get "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ABABBBB"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"1706A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1706/problem/A"}